# King T'Challa: "{4}{W}{U}: Transform King T'Challa. Activate only as a sorcery." In Bot1's turn-3 upkeep, with seven
# mana at hand, the ability is not offered (CR 602.5d: only in a main phase of its controller's turn with the stack
# empty); in the main phase it is (the positive control). The permanent becomes Black Panther, Hope Enduring, a 3/3 with
# flash and double strike (CR 712.18: the same object, so it can attack - it has been under Bot1's control since turn 1).
# It attacks: "Whenever Black Panther deals combat damage to a player, draw a card" triggers in the first-strike and the
# regular combat damage step each (CR 702.4b, 510.4): Bot2 loses 6 and Bot1 draws two cards. King T'Challa's draw trigger
# is gone with the front face (CR 712.8e), so Bot1's second card of the turn draws nothing more. Its prevention comes
# with the back face: on turn 4 Bot2's Lightning Bolt at it is prevented, where it killed the front face
# (king-tchalla-front-face-is-dealt-damage-and-dies-to-a-lightning-bolt).

